[2m[2mSession[0m: [1;33mdeepseek_deepseek-v4-flash-integration-bug-trial-3[0m[0m
**Fix: `checkout.py:13-30`**

Two bugs, one root cause: a **TOCTOU race** between `check_stock` and `decrement`, with a payment in between. Concurrent coroutines all see the same initial stock in `check_stock`, proceed to payment, then race on `decrement` — losers are charged but get no item.

**What changed:** Reversed the order. `decrement` runs first (atomically reserves stock — the check-and-subtract is synchronous with no `await` in between), so only one coroutine can claim each item. Then `charge`. If charge fails, `increment` releases the reservation.

**Verified:** 10/10 runs — zero ghost charges, zero negative inventory, charge totals always match successful orders.
